  "id": "Compound::DB02300 - Gene::7421",
  "verbalization": "Calcipotriol, a vitamin D analog, is implicated in the regulation of the Vitamin D Receptor (Vdr) through multiple mechanistic pathways. The evidence suggests that Calcipotriol interacts with Vdr via direct binding, as indicated by its interaction with Cyp24a1 and its role in the Vitamin D Receptor Signaling Pathway. Additionally, Calcipotriol is linked to Vdr through its resemblance to dihydrotachysterol and calcidiol, which both bind to Vdr. These relationships are supported by the lowest common ancestors of Calcipotriol and its analogs, which all converge on the hydroxy secosteroid class and ultimately on Vitamin D. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Calcipotriol modulates Vdr activity, likely through the regulation of vitamin D metabolism. The evidence supports a direct interaction between Calcipotriol and Vdr, with the observed scores reflecting the strength of these relationships.",
